# fixedbugs, defect 2336, 2026-11-08: a record's fields were found by name by
# walking all of them at every read, in the checker (`check/access.hero`, and
# `check/field_names.hero` for `Wide::f0`) and again in the lowering
# (`ir/layout.hero`), so a record of N fields each read once cost the square
# of N. Each holder's names are now read into a table at its first read and
# asked after (`named_fields.hero`). `heroes check` on N fields each read
# once, at 1,024, 2,048, 4,096 and 8,192: 1.41, 4.03, 13.23 and 47.46
# billion instructions before, 0.77, 1.45, 2.82 and 5.56 after; the
# lowering besides, `build --dump-ir` at 1,024 to 4,096: 5.95, 20.30 and
# 75.07 before, 1.62, 3.00 and 5.79 after. This program, 2,048 fields read
# once each and named once each, sums what every read and every name finds:
# `check` 13.15 billion before and 3.18 after, `--dump-ir` 31.48 and 6.87.
record Wide
    f0: i64
    f1: i64
    f2: i64
    f3: i64
    f4: i64
    f5: i64
